### =====================================================================
### Topic 8: three apps. Start: registry (8761) -> catalog (8081) -> enrollment (8082)
### Eureka dashboard: http://localhost:8761
### =====================================================================

### Ask the catalog DIRECTLY (by address)
GET http://localhost:8081/catalog/courses

### Enroll: the enrollment service finds "catalog-service" through Eureka, calls it with Feign -> CONFIRMED (201)
POST http://localhost:8082/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "student": "ada", "courseCode": "CS101" }

### Another one: start a 2nd catalog on port 8091 and send this a few times. Watch servedByCatalogPort!
POST http://localhost:8082/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "student": "tunde", "courseCode": "CLOUD1" }

### A course that doesn't exist -> 400 (the catalog answered 404, a NORMAL answer)
POST http://localhost:8082/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "student": "musa", "courseCode": "MAGIC999" }

### Now STOP every catalog app (Ctrl + C) and send this -> PENDING (202) from the FALLBACK
POST http://localhost:8082/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "student": "chioma", "courseCode": "CS102" }

### All enrollments kept by the enrollment service
GET http://localhost:8082/enrollments

### Health of each service (Actuator, from Topic 7)
GET http://localhost:8082/actuator/health
